  "Question": "A ream of paper containing \\(500\\) sheets is \\(5\\) cm thick. Approximately how many sheets of this type of paper would there be in a stack \\(7.5\\) cm high?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(250\\)",
    "B": "\\(550\\)",
    "C": "\\(667\\)",
    "D": "\\(750\\)",
    "E": "\\(1250\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "For this estimate, use the same thickness per sheet throughout the stack. Then the number of sheets is proportional to the stack's height. A \\(1\\)-cm stack contains approximately\n\\[\n500\\div5=100\\text{ sheets}.\n\\]\nTherefore a \\(7.5\\)-cm stack contains approximately \\(7.5\\times100=750\\) sheets, choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
